cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SmallField: GPU conformer generation with ETKDG and MMFF94"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.3.0
authors:
  - given-names: Ash
    family-names: Vardanian
    email: 1983160+ashvardanian@users.noreply.github.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/unum-science/SmallField"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  SmallField generates 3D molecular conformers from SMILES strings on the GPU,
  combining ETKDG distance geometry with Cambridge Structural Database torsion
  preferences and MMFF94 optimization. Geometries, energies, and torsion
  matching are cross-validated term by term against RDKit, so the speedup is an
  implementation result rather than a change of method.

  One molecule is assigned to a single CUDA warp and its entire optimization is
  kept in on-chip memory. Reduced-precision representations of the intermediate
  state, most notably a quantized distance-bounds matrix, are what make that
  residency possible: throughput comes from occupancy rather than from
  approximating the physics. Output is reproducible bitwise under a fixed seed,
  and the library deliberately answers one question — given a SMILES string,
  produce K geometries consistent with it.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - conformer generation
  - distance geometry
  - ETKDG
  - MMFF94
  - molecular mechanics
  - SMILES
  - shape descriptors
  - virtual screening
  - CUDA
  - GPU
